{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run/draft/update.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"rationale\": \"Review the retained membership-level promotion control. The matching target is accepted and promotes the observer; different and empty targets are rejected and retain the observer role. The control confirms the implementation behavior but does not decide whether the API comment or the membership guard is the intended contract. Consolidate it with the existing source mismatch while keeping the finding scoped as lower-severity client behavior.\",\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@observer-promotion-target-control\",\n      \"kind\": \"fact\",\n      \"statement\": \"In the membership control, an observer at address a2 is promoted when the AddNode target is a2. Targets a3 and empty are rejected, and the observer role remains after both rejections.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"Internal membership state machine with OrderedConfigChange enabled; fresh membership per case; observer 100 at a2; AddNode at index 1000; test-only direct invocation, no NodeHost target validator or transport.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"membership-promote-guard\",\n        \"membership-config-accept\",\n        \"promotion-match-test\",\n        \"promotion-mismatch-test\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {\n        \"7dc00e103f9d43e9b4e73536922acae7\": [\n          1,\n          3,\n          5\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"interpretations\": [\n    {\n      \"investigation_id\": \"7034811e609340afbfc17ad24f2fc632-question-0\",\n      \"experiment_id\": \"90f787d3f2b44fbd9217e785b2fd7787-experiment\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"request-addnode-contract\",\n        \"request-config-validate\",\n        \"membership-promote-guard\",\n        \"membership-config-accept\",\n        \"promotion-match-test\",\n        \"promotion-mismatch-test\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {\n        \"7dc00e103f9d43e9b4e73536922acae7\": [\n          1,\n          3,\n          5\n        ]\n      },\n      \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n      \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The client-contract mismatch is now supported by both source and a retained membership control. The RequestAddNode comment says target is ignored when an existing observer is promoted. requestConfigChange validates every non-remove target and rejects an empty or invalid value with ErrInvalidAddress. At the membership layer, a different valid target does not satisfy isPromoteObserver and is rejected by isInvalidObserverPromotion; only an address equal to the stored observer address is accepted. The control confirms the observable endpoints: target a2 is accepted and promotes observer 100; target a3 and empty are rejected, with the observer role retained. The implementation's address-equality guard is intentional according to TestIsInvalidObserverPromotion and the matching-address success in TestAddNodeCanPromoteObserverToNode. Thus a caller following the documented ignored-target invocation can receive an immediate error or a rejected config change, while a caller who passes the observer's exact address succeeds. This is a client-contract/documentation or API-behavior mismatch, not a demonstrated CFT safety or unbounded-liveness defect for a matching-address promotion. The evidence does not establish whether the API comment should be corrected or the target handling changed.\",\n      \"knowledge\": [\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"7034811e609340afbfc17ad24f2fc632-knowledge-0\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n          \"assertion\": \"Promotion requires the observer's stored address; empty, invalid, or different targets do not follow the documented ignored-target path.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"@observer-promotion-target-control\",\n          \"revision\": 1,\n          \"assertion\": \"The control accepted only the matching address and retained the observer role for the rejected targets.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"The matching-address control accepted the promotion and removed the observer role, so the operation is available with the stored address.\",\n        \"The source and existing test deliberately reject a different address, indicating the address-equality guard is intentional.\",\n        \"The control starts at the membership state machine and does not include the request-level validator, so it confirms code behavior rather than the full documented client path.\"\n      ],\n      \"limitations\": [\n        \"The control does not execute NodeHost RequestAddNode or a custom target validator.\",\n        \"It does not resolve whether the API comment or the membership guard is normative.\",\n        \"The mismatch is lower-severity client behavior; it does not establish a CFT safety or unbounded-liveness defect for a matching-address promotion.\",\n        \"No transport, persistence, restart, or concurrent membership transition was exercised.\"\n      ],\n      \"joint_history\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
