e-tagging occurs between that send and node 2's consumer in the main probe.\",\n          \"The main reply's log index was 4 and the ready index was 4, so neither the main nor timeout execution shows a stale committed index or stale application state.\",\n          \"The late context-101 confirmation produced zero context-correct replies and completion remained zero.\"\n        ],\n        \"counterevidence_omitted_count\": 3,\n        \"limitations\": [\n          \"The ILogDB is test-only and in-memory; disk failure, restart, snapshots, and real transport delay were not exercised.\",\n          \"The main test applies the returned ready index synchronously; the companion timeout receipt measures the logical deadline at tick 51, not wall-clock scheduling.\",\n          \"Observer-originated reads are measured only at the leader-side reply; the observer NodeHost forwarding and pending-read consumer are source-traced but not measured. Other membership layouts were not measured.\"\n        ],\n        \"limitations_omitted_count\": 2,\n        \"joint_history\": \"The follower, control, and timeout receipts come from the same three-peer in-memory harness family; the observer receipt uses a focused internal Raft leader with voters {1,2,3} and observer 4. All four experiments are under the same ReadIndex investigation and exercise the same leader-side confirmation path. The follower and observer cases both queue an earlier remote context before a later voter  [preview: 296 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n        \"failure_attribution\": null,\n        \"operation_id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"interpretations\",\n          \"id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5-interpretation-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"view\": \"preview\",\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n        \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-question-0\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-question-0\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"question\": \"Can a delayed HeartbeatResp from a node that has left the voter set satisfy a current ReadIndex quorum under legal configuration transitions?\",\n      \"hypothesis\": \"Because lw accepts observer heartbeat responses and readIndex.confirm counts any from value, a delayed voter heartbeat response might count after the node becomes an observer.\",\n      \"discriminator\": \"\",\n      \"disposition\": \"explained\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"leader-heartbeat-resp\",\n        \"lw-remote-lookup\",\n        \"broadcast-heartbeat-hint\",\n        \"peer-response-filter\",\n        \"readindex-confirm\",\n        \"membership-add-existing\",\n        \"membership-add-removed\",\n        \"membership-becoming-observer\",\n        \"membership-handle-config-change\",\n        \"raft-remove-node\",\n        \"raft-restore-role-guard\"\n      ],\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"knowledge\": [],\n      \"open_gaps\": [],\n      \"latest_execution\": null,\n      \"latest_interpretation\": {\n        \"id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-interpretation-0\",\n        \"investigation_id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-question-0\",\n        \"experiment_id\": null,\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"leader-heartbeat-resp\",\n          \"lw-remote-lookup\",\n          \"broadcast-heartbeat-hint\",\n          \"peer-response-filter\",\n          \"readindex-confirm\",\n          \"membership-add-existing\",\n          \"membership-add-removed\",\n          \"membership-becoming-observer\",\n          \"membership-handle-config-change\",\n          \"raft-remove-node\",\n          \"raft-restore-role-guard\"\n        ],\n        \"executions\": {},\n        \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n        \"defect_claim\": \"refuted\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The suspicion is refuted for the captured legal paths, although the low-level code alone would count it. handleLeaderHeartbeatResp confirms when a heartbeat response carries a nonzero hint, lw admits observer responses, and readIndex.confirm counts the responding node without checking whether it is currently a voter. That is the plausible weakness. The legal transition path does not create the nee [preview: 984 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n        \"answers\": {},\n        \"knowledge\": [\n          {\n            \"entry_id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-knowledge-0\",\n            \"revision\": 1,\n            \"assertion\": \"Legal transitions prevent a former voter from retaining a voter-issued nonzero ReadIndex context as an observer.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"The low-level path does not check voter eligibility in readIndex.confirm; it counts any nonzero-hint response that lw admits.\",\n          \"Observers are admitted by lw for heartbeat responses and are not filtered out by readIndex.confirm.\",\n          \"The refutation depends on the legal membership guards and nonzero-hint routing, not on the absence of these low-level behaviors.\"\n        ],\n        \"limitations\": [\n          \"Direct mutation of the raft role maps, an operator restarting a node with a role inconsistent with cluster membership, forged heartbeat responses, or a custom transport that changes admission are excluded.\",\n          \"This source-only account does not run an execution; it relies on the captured membership and raft control flow.\",\n          \"The established main finding remains separate: a legal follower-originated ReadIndex batch can receive another request's context and fail to complete.\"\n        ],\n        \"joint_history\": \"\",\n        \"failure_attribution\": null,\n        \"operation_id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907\",\n        \"view\": \"previe