     \"Context validity and authority transitions\"\n    ],\n    \"target\": {\n      \"repo\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/dragonboat\",\n      \"snapshot_id\": \"0917893e9a6d4b5f8bf6b7752319db78\"\n    },\n    \"directed_question\": null,\n    \"questions\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-question-0\",\n        \"question\": \"When the leader confirms a later queued ReadIndex context before an earlier follower's context, does each follower receive a reply tagged with the SystemCtx it admitted, and can its pending read complete?\",\n        \"disposition\": \"explained\",\n        \"parent_id\": null,\n        \"discriminator\": \"The retained execution's readindex_reply context and read_completion_state for the earlier request. A later source path or delivery rule that re-tags the reply by request identity, or completes the original batch despite the mismatched key, would change the judgment.\",\n        \"resume_conditions\": [],\n        \"open_gap_count\": 0,\n        \"latest_interpretation\": {\n          \"id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5-interpretation-0\",\n          \"conclusion\": \"violated\",\n          \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The current conclusion remains a bounded liveness and client-contract defect for remote ReadIndex requests when a later queued context is confirmed first. The follower receipt admits node 2's context {101,1002} and node 3's context {202,2003}; event 2 replies to node 2 with node 3's context and log index 4; event 3 leaves node 2's original batch at index zero after the real ready index 4 was appli [preview: 1510 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n          \"counterevidence_count\": 6,\n          \"limitation_count\": 5,\n          \"view\": \"preview\",\n          \"record\": {\n            \"path\": \"state.json\",\n            \"collection\": \"interpretations\",\n            \"id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5-interpretation-0\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n          \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-question-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-question-0\",\n        \"question\": \"Can a delayed HeartbeatResp from a node that has left the voter set satisfy a current ReadIndex quorum under legal configuration transitions?\",\n        \"disposition\": \"explained\",\n        \"parent_id\": null,\n        \"discriminator\": \"\",\n        \"resume_conditions\": [],\n        \"open_gap_count\": 0,\n        \"latest_interpretation\": {\n          \"id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-interpretation-0\",\n          \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n          \"defect_claim\": \"refuted\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The suspicion is refuted for the captured legal paths, although the low-level code alone would count it. handleLeaderHeartbeatResp confirms when a heartbeat response carries a nonzero hint, lw admits observer responses, and readIndex.confirm counts the responding node without checking whether it is currently a voter. That is the plausible weakness. The legal transition path does not create the nee [preview: 984 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n          \"counterevidence_count\": 3,\n          \"limitation_count\": 3,\n          \"view\": \"preview\",\n          \"record\": {\n            \"path\": \"state.json\",\n            \"collection\": \"interpretations\",\n            \"id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-interpretation-0\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n          \"id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-question-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7034811e609340afbfc17ad24f2fc632-question-0\",\n        \"question\": \"Does RequestAddNode's documented ignored target allow an observer to be promoted with an empty or different target?\",\n        \"disposition\": \"explained\",\n        \"parent_id\": null,\n        \"discriminator\": \"\",\n        \"resume_conditions\": [],\n        \"open_gap_count\": 0,\n        \"latest_interpretation\": {\n          \"id\": \"c5b7c76791cb4a1da22e4fada40d9ed8-interpretation-0\",\n          \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n          \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The client-contract mismatch is now supported by both source and a retained membership control. The RequestAddNode comment says target is ignored when an existing observer is promoted. requestConfigChange validates every non-remove target and rejects an empty or invalid value with ErrInvalidAddress. At the membership layer, a different valid target does not satisfy isPromoteObserver and is rejecte [preview: 894 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n          \"counterevidence_count\": 3,\n          \"limitation_count\": 4,\n          \"view\": \"preview\",\n          \"record\": {\n            \"path\": \"state.json\",\n            \"collection\": \"interpretations\",\n            \"id\": \"c5b7c76791cb4a1da22e4fada40d9ed8-interpretation-0\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n          \"id\": \"7034811e609340afbfc17ad24f2fc632-question-0\"\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"knowledge\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n        \"statement\": \"readIndex.confirm(ctx, from, quorum) confirms every queued request up to and including ctx and returns each queued readStatus with its original SystemCtx, while rewriting each returned index to the confirmed request's committed index and deleting all returned entries from the queue.\",\n        \"conditions\": \"The leader has multiple pending ReadIndex requests, ctx names a later queued request, and quorum confirmations are received for ctx.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-1\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n        \"statement\": \"handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation adds a local ready-to-read result with each readStatus's own ctx, but for a remote s.from it emits ReadIndexResp using the confirming heartbeat's Hint and HintHigh instead of s.ctx.\",\n        \"conditions\": \"readIndex.confirm returns at least one remote readStatus whose ctx differs from the confirming heartbeat's context.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-1\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-2\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n        \"statement\": \"The node registers a pending read batch under a generated SystemCtx. pendingReadIndex.addReady updates only a batch whose map key equals the response SystemCtx, and pendingReadIndex.applied completes only a batch with a nonzero ready index not exceeding the applied index. An unmatched response leaves the original batch at index zero.\",\n        \"conditions\": \"A follower-originated read is registered before a response is processed, and the response SystemCtx differs from the registered key.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-2\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"083048b436e74eaa9a8ec611b31527e4-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"fact\",\n        \"statement\": \"In the exercised three-voter group, when two follower-originated ReadIndex requests with distinct SystemCtx values were queued and the later context was confirmed first, node 2 received a ReadIndex reply carrying node 3's context. Node 2's original admitted batch still existed at index zero after the real ReadyToRead index 4 was applied, and the later context-101 confirmation produced no context-c [preview: 13 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n        \"conditions\": \"Three real in-process Raft Peer handlers with bootstrap membership {1,2,3}; node 1 leader; node 2 and node 3 follower-originated ReadIndex requests with distinct contexts; the later context's heartbeat was delivered to node 3 and its confirmation returned to the leader before the earlier heartbeat reached node 2; the test-only in-memory ILogDB and controlled logical delivery order were used; produ [preview: 25 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"083048b436e74eaa9a8ec611b31527e4-knowledge-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"fact\",\n        \"statement\": \"Under the captured legal membership and raft paths, a node that is a current voter cannot become an observer or witness while retaining its voter role: adding a current address as observer or witness is rejected, removal deletes the node from every role map and marks it removed, re-adding a removed ID is rejected, and restoring a snapshot panics if a full member appears in the observer or witness  [preview: 247 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n        \"conditions\": \"The user-facing configuration-change and raft snapshot paths are used as captured; no direct mutation of internal role maps, operator role misconfiguration, forged messages, or a custom transport that changes response admission is included.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"7e17be3eac204967962a1e20e3dfc907-knowledge-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"1457862374ac4b5bbba3c0e3588dbb50-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"fact\",\n        \"statement\": \"In the same three-peer in-process harness, when node 2's admitted ReadIndex context was confirmed first, the leader's reply carried that same context, the real follower handler's ReadyToRead was consumed by pendingReadIndex, whose batch index became 4, and the admitted client read completed after the ready index was applied.\",\n        \"conditions\": \"Real in-process Raft Peer handlers with bootstrap membership {1,2,3}; test-only in-memory ILogDB; two queued contexts; node 2's context confirmed first; node 2's reply routed through its real follower handler and pendingReadIndex consumer; production code unchanged.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"1457862374ac4b5bbba3c0e3588dbb50-knowledge-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"cd8b5340c6da42b49b1358c1b1420aa6-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"fact\",\n        \"statement\": \"In the logical-deadline case, after node 2 received the later context's reply and the real ready index was applied, the original read batch remained at index zero and did not complete before the 50-tick deadline. At logical tick 51 the pendingReadIndex GC returned RequestTimeout and removed the batch.\",\n        \"conditions\": \"Same three-peer in-process harness and later-first context ordering; a test-only in-memory ILogDB; node 2's request created with a 50-tick timeout; the applied ready index was supplied before the logical clock was advanced to 51; production code unchanged.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"cd8b5340c6da42b49b1358c1b1420aa6-knowledge-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"68dce962924a4244bd9688bff78649ed-knowledge-1\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n        \"statement\": \"handleLeaderReadIndex rejects a witness source but does not reject an observer source; it queues the request in the same readIndex path and broadcasts the confirmation heartbeat to voting members. An observer's local ReadIndex is forwarded by handleObserverReadIndex to handleFollowerReadIndex, and its response is routed through handleObserverReadIndexResp to handleFollowerReadIndexResp and the sam [preview: 28 characters omitted; see full record]\",\n        \"conditions\": \"The observer has a known leader, the leader has a committed entry in its current term, and the leader accepts the queued request. This is a source trace; observer-originated reads were not executed in the retained receipts.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"68dce962924a4244bd9688bff78649ed-knowledge-1\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"fact\",\n        \"statement\": \"In the leader-side observer case, observer 4 admitted ReadIndex context {101,1002}; voter 3's later context {202,2003} was confirmed first; the ReadIndex reply addressed to observer 4 carried {202,2003} with log index 1, and the leader's pending ReadIndex queue was empty.\",\n        \"conditions\": \"Real internal/raft handlers with voting members {1,2,3} and a test-only observer map entry for node 4; a committed current-term no-op; observer-originated ReadIndex context A and voter-originated later context B queued; voter 3's heartbeat response for B delivered first; no NodeHost observer forwarding or pending-read consumer in this leader-side experiment.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5-knowledge-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"7034811e609340afbfc17ad24f2fc632-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"fact\",\n        \"statement\": \"RequestAddNode promotes an existing observer only when the supplied AddNode address equals the observer's stored address. An invalid or empty target is rejected by requestConfigChange before a proposal; a different valid target is rejected by membership.isInvalidObserverPromotion. A matching address is accepted and removes the observer role.\",\n        \"conditions\": \"The user-facing RequestAddNode path, the default or configured target validator, and the membership state machine are used as captured. No execution is included; the behavior is established by the source and membership tests.\",\n        \"view\": \"preview\",\n        \"record\": {\n          \"path\": \"state.json\",\n          \"collection\": \"knowledge\",\n          \"id\": \"7034811e609340afbfc17ad24f2fc632-knowledge-0\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"c5b7c76791cb4a1da22e4fada40d9ed8-knowledge-0\",\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"kind\": \"fact\",\n        \"statement\": \"In the membership control, an observer at address a2 is promoted when the AddNode target is a2. Targets a3 and empty are rejected, and the observer role remains after both rejections.\",\n        \"conditions\": \"Internal membership state machine with OrderedConfigChange enabled; fresh membership per case; obs