{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\niv=[x for x in s['interpretations'] if x['id'].startswith('84ba0b5')][0]\nprint(json.dumps(iv, indent=1))\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5-interpretation-0\",\n \"investigation_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-question-0\",\n \"experiment_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-experiment\",\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"readindex-confirm-handler\",\n  \"readindex-confirm\",\n  \"readindex-test-context\",\n  \"pending-read-addready\",\n  \"pending-read-applied\",\n  \"pending-read-gc\",\n  \"follower-readindexresp\",\n  \"node-process-ready\",\n  \"node-readindex-admission\",\n  \"systemctx-identity\",\n  \"leader-readindex-admission\",\n  \"observer-readindex-forward\",\n  \"follower-readindex-forward\"\n ],\n \"executions\": {\n  \"c2848ac1c82f442ba305267049bbb53b\": [\n   2,\n   3,\n   4\n  ],\n  \"55e578441ac24bde9e837485d2c078a6\": [\n   1,\n   2\n  ],\n  \"c414588b5bc24b189d3df3217e37d7b7\": [\n   1\n  ],\n  \"4e011b84ec9241da9022ce3b300b5948\": [\n   1\n  ]\n },\n \"conclusion\": \"violated\",\n \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n \"rationale\": \"The current conclusion remains a bounded liveness and client-contract defect for remote ReadIndex requests when a later queued context is confirmed first. The follower receipt admits node 2's context {101,1002} and node 3's context {202,2003}; event 2 replies to node 2 with node 3's context and log index 4; event 3 leaves node 2's original batch at index zero after the real ready index 4 was applied; event 4 shows the later context-101 confirmation produces no context-correct reply and no completion. The source cause remains handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation using the confirming heartbeat's Hint/HintHigh instead of the queued request's s.ctx, while confirm deletes the earlier queue entry and pendingReadIndex.addReady requires an exact SystemCtx key. The sequential control confirms the same consumer path with node 2's admitted context first: its reply carries that context and completion is 1 with batch index 4. The logical-deadline case keeps the later-first ordering: its event 1 records original_batch_index zero, no completion before the 50-tick deadline, RequestTimeout at advanced tick 51, and the stale batch absent after GC. The observer leader-side experiment admits observer 4's context A, queues voter 3's later context B, confirms B first, and observes the reply addressed to observer 4 carrying B with log index 1; this measures the same leader-side substitution for an observer source. Together the receipts distinguish a context-association defect from a general consumer or harness failure, measure the bounded follower endpoint, and extend the leader-side reply defect to observer sources. The main reply's log index is a later committed index, so no stale-read value or safety violation is established. The main request remains uncompleted after a valid applied index until the measured logical timeout; the observer's local pending-read consumer and completion were not measured.\",\n \"answers\": {},\n \"knowledge\": [\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The confirming context returns earlier queued requests while preserving each request's own SystemCtx.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-1\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"Remote replies are tagged with the confirming heartbeat context instead of the queued request's context.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-knowledge-2\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"A response with a nonmatching SystemCtx leaves the original pending batch at index zero and cannot complete it.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"083048b436e74eaa9a8ec611b31527e4-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The exercised later-confirmation ordering produced a mismatched reply context and left the earlier read batch unready after the ready index was applied.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"1457862374ac4b5bbba3c0e3588dbb50-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The sequential-confirmation control completed when the admitted context was confirmed first.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"cd8b5340c6da42b49b1358c1b1420aa6-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The logical-deadline case returned RequestTimeout at tick 51 and removed the stale batch.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"68dce962924a4244bd9688bff78649ed-knowledge-1\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"Observer-originated ReadIndex requests enter the same leader queue and pending-read response path.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The observer leader-side reply carried the later confirming context rather than the observer's admitted context.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"The source path that constructs the remote reply uses m.Hint and m.HintHigh; no re-tagging occurs between that send and node 2's consumer in the main probe.\",\n  \"The main reply's log index was 4 and the ready index was 4, so neither the main nor timeout execution shows a stale committed index or stale application state.\",\n  \"The late context-101 confirmation produced zero context-correct replies and completion remained zero.\",\n  \"The sequential control completed with the admitted context, so the main failure is not a general inability of the harness or pending-read consumer to complete.\",\n  \"The timeout receipt shows a client timeout and cleanup, not a successful stale read; it measures the bounded endpoint without establishing a safety violation.\",\n  \"The observer experiment measures only the leader-side reply context; it does not execute the observer's local forwarding or pending-read completion.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"The ILogDB is test-only and in-memory; disk failure, restart, snapshots, and real transport delay were not exercised.\",\n  \"The main test applies the returned ready index synchronously; the companion timeout receipt measures the logical deadline at tick 51, not wall-clock scheduling.\",\n  \"Observer-originated reads are measured only at the leader-side reply; the observer NodeHost forwarding and pending-read consumer are source-traced but not measured. Other membership layouts were not measured.\",\n  \"The sequential control holds only for its exercised first-context ordering; it does not establish safety or completion for all schedules.\",\n  \"The observed wrong reply context is a correlation defect; it is not by itself evidence that the returned read index is stale or that a wrong data value was read.\"\n ],\n \"joint_history\": \"The follower, control, and timeout receipts come from the same three-peer in-memory harness family; the observer receipt uses a focused internal Raft leader with voters {1,2,3} and observer 4. All four experiments are under the same ReadIndex investigation and exercise the same leader-side confirmation path. The follower and observer cases both queue an earlier remote context before a later voter context and confirm the later one first; the control confirms the admitted context first; the timeout repeats the later-first ordering and advances the pending-read logical clock. The observer case does not include the observer's local consumer, so its result is limited to the leader-side reply.\",\n \"failure_attribution\": null,\n \"operation_id\": \"84ba0b5abd3a42c5866eb46354c561b5\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor e in s['experiments']:\n    b=e['basis']\n    print('===', e['id'])\n    print('req:', b.get('requirement'))\n    print('resp:', b.get('responsibility'))\n    print('comparisons:', json.dumps(b.get('comparisons'), indent=1)[:2500])\n    print('prereqs:', json.dumps(b.get('prerequisites'), indent=1)[:800])\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nfor e in s['experiments']:\n    b=e['basis']\n    print('===', e['id'])\n    print('req:', b.get('requirement'))\n    print('resp:', b.get('responsibility'))\n    print('comparisons:', json.dumps(b.get('comparisons'), indent=1)[:2500])\n    print('prereqs:', json.dumps(b.get('prerequisites'), indent=1)[:800])\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"=== 827f420be72d403f9a804a543fac77cc-experiment\nreq: A follower-originated ReadIndex decision must be associated with the SystemCtx under which that follower registered the pending read, and a returned ReadyToRead at an applied index must complete that pending batch. Confirmation batching at the leader must not replace a remote request's context with another request's context.\nresp: The leader constructs remote ReadIndexResp messages in handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation. The requesting node's pendingReadIndex consumes the returned SystemCtx and associates it with the registered batch. The test uses real Peer and pending-read handlers; it controls only message ordering and the test storage backend.\ncomparisons: [\n {\n  \"event\": \"readindex_reply\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"response_ctx_low\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": null,\n   \"reference\": \"admitted.ctx_low\"\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [\n   {\n    \"field\": \"reply_to\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 2,\n    \"reference\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"field\": \"trigger_from\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 3,\n    \"reference\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"The ReadIndex reply delivered to node 2 must carry the context node 2 admitted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"event\": \"read_completion_state\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"completed_after_response\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": 1,\n   \"reference\": null\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [\n   {\n    \"field\": \"original_batch_exists\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": true,\n    \"reference\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"field\": \"ready_index_applied\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": true,\n    \"reference\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"After the real ready index is applied, the admitted pending read should complete; zero means the response was not associated with the original batch.\"\n }\n]\nprereqs: null\n=== c899574eabad4149aa0bed6d7530c411-experiment\nreq: When the admitted context is the one confirmed first, the remote reply must carry that same SystemCtx and the applied ReadyToRead must complete the pending read through the same consumer path.\nresp: The leader constructs the ReadIndex response in handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation; the requesting node's real follower handler and pendingReadIndex consume it. The control keeps the production handlers and changes only the order in which the two legal confirmations are delivered.\ncomparisons: [\n {\n  \"event\": \"control_readindex_reply\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"control_admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"response_ctx_low\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": null,\n   \"reference\": \"control_admitted.ctx_low\"\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [\n   {\n    \"field\": \"reply_to\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 2,\n    \"reference\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"field\": \"trigger_from\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 2,\n    \"reference\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"The control reply must carry the context node 2 admitted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"event\": \"control_read_completion_state\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"control_admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"completed_after_response\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": 1,\n   \"reference\": null\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [\n   {\n    \"field\": \"original_batch_exists\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": true,\n    \"reference\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"field\": \"ready_index_applied\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": true,\n    \"reference\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"The admitted read should complete when its own context is confirmed and its ready index is applied.\"\n }\n]\nprereqs: null\n=== f1a0a11d093845dcad0e2960a52a98b4-experiment\nreq: The earlier unmatched batch must remain uncompleted before the caller deadline and must yield the caller-supplied timeout result after the logical deadline; the GC path must remove the stale batch.\nresp: pendingReadIndex.gc owns the deadline timeout and batch cleanup after the response context fails to match the admitted batch. The test uses the real pending-read consumer and only advances its logical clock.\ncomparisons: [\n {\n  \"event\": \"wrong_context_timeout_state\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"timeout_admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"result_code_is_timeout\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": true,\n   \"reference\": null\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [\n   {\n    \"field\": \"original_batch_exists\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": true,\n    \"reference\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"field\": \"completed_before_deadline\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 0,\n    \"reference\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"field\": \"deadline_tick\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 50,\n    \"reference\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"field\": \"advanced_tick\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 51,\n    \"reference\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"After the logical deadline and the GC trigger, the unmatched pending read must return RequestTimeout.\"\n },\n {\n  \"event\": \"wrong_context_timeout_state\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"timeout_admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"batch_still_present_after_gc\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": false,\n   \"reference\": null\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [\n   {\n    \"field\": \"result_code_is_timeout\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": true,\n    \"reference\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"The timeout GC path should remove the stale batch.\"\n }\n]\nprereqs: null\n=== 79a0cadfd8b94b3ea070c6cce62864ee-experiment\nreq: An observer-originated ReadIndex reply must carry the SystemCtx admitted by that observer. The leader's ReadIndex queue and context handling must not be follower-only.\nresp: handleLeaderReadIndex admits the observer request and handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation constructs the remote reply; the test exercises those real handlers and only controls message ordering.\ncomparisons: [\n {\n  \"event\": \"observer_readindex_reply\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"observer_admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"response_ctx_low\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": null,\n   \"reference\": \"observer_admitted.ctx_low\"\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [\n   {\n    \"field\": \"reply_to\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 4,\n    \"reference\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"field\": \"trigger_from\",\n    \"op\": \"eq\",\n    \"value\": 3,\n    \"reference\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"The observer's reply must carry the context the observer admitted.\"\n }\n]\nprereqs: null\n=== 90f787d3f2b44fbd9217e785b2fd7787-experiment\nreq: The membership state machine must accept an AddNode only when it promotes the observer with the stored address; a different or empty target must not promote the observer or remove its observer role.\nresp: membership.handleConfigChange and its promotion guards own the decision; this control invokes that state machine directly and records its returns and role map.\ncomparisons: [\n {\n  \"event\": \"promotion_target_decision\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"accepted\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": null,\n   \"reference\": \"admitted.expected\"\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n  \"description\": \"The membership accepted decision should match the target-case expectation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"event\": \"promotion_target_decision\",\n  \"identity_fields\": [\n   \"request_id\"\n  ],\n  \"admission_alias\": \"admitted\",\n  \"assertion\": {\n   \"field\": \"observer_role_retained\",\n   \"op\": \"eq\",\n   \"value\": null,\n   \"reference\": \"admitted.expected_retained\"\n  },\n  \"antecedent\": null,\n  \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n  \"description\": \"The observer role should be retained exactly when the promotion is not accepted.\"\n }\n]\nprereqs: null\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
